§ `s 254 -- merger or consolidation of domestic corporations and joint-stock or other associations`

§§ `s 254(a) the terms the section defines`

-- "joint-stock association" (src:1148): any association of the kind commonly known as a joint-stock association or joint-stock
-- company, and any unincorporated association, trust or enterprise having members or having outstanding shares of stock or other
-- evidences of financial or beneficial interest, formed by agreement, under statutory authority or otherwise, under the laws of this
-- State or any other jurisdiction -- "but does not include a corporation, partnership or limited liability company". The core's
-- `a joint-stock association` is the first kind; a trust or other unincorporated business is one if it has members or interests.
-- src:1148 | The term “joint-stock association” as used in this section, includes any association of the kind commonly known as a joint-stock association or joint-stock company and any unincorporated association, trust or enterprise having members or having outstanding shares of stock or other evidences of financial or beneficial interest therein, whether formed or organized by agreement or under statutory authority or otherwise and whether formed or organized under the laws of this State or any other jurisdiction, but does not include a corporation, partnership or limited liability company. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 254(a) (src:1148)
GIVEN kind                                                                                                IS A `Kind of entity`
      `it has members, or has outstanding shares of stock or other evidences of financial or beneficial interest` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 254(a) the kind of entity is a joint-stock association` kind `it has members, or has outstanding shares of stock or other evidences of financial or beneficial interest` MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `a joint-stock association`                        THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a statutory trust`                                THEN `it has members, or has outstanding shares of stock or other evidences of financial or beneficial interest`
    WHEN `a business trust or association`                  THEN `it has members, or has outstanding shares of stock or other evidences of financial or beneficial interest`
    WHEN `a real estate investment trust`                   THEN `it has members, or has outstanding shares of stock or other evidences of financial or beneficial interest`
    WHEN `a common-law trust`                               THEN `it has members, or has outstanding shares of stock or other evidences of financial or beneficial interest`
    WHEN `any other unincorporated business or association` THEN `it has members, or has outstanding shares of stock or other evidences of financial or beneficial interest`
    WHEN `a natural person`                                 THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a corporation` k                                  THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a general partnership`                            THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a limited partnership`                            THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a limited liability partnership`                  THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a limited liability limited partnership`          THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a limited liability company`                      THEN FALSE

-- "stockholder" as used in this section includes every member of such a joint-stock association or holder of a share of stock or
-- other evidence of financial or beneficial interest in it: "includes" widens the ordinary meaning, it does not replace it.
-- src:1148 | includes every member of such joint-stock association or holder of a share of stock or other evidence of financial or beneficial interest therein.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 254(a) (src:1148)
GIVEN `the person is a stockholder in the ordinary sense, a holder of stock of a corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a member of the joint-stock association`                                  IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person holds a share of stock or other evidence of financial or beneficial interest in the joint-stock association` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 254(a) the person is a stockholder for the purposes of s 254` `the person is a stockholder in the ordinary sense, a holder of stock of a corporation` `the person is a member of the joint-stock association` `the person holds a share of stock or other evidence of financial or beneficial interest in the joint-stock association` MEANS
        `the person is a stockholder in the ordinary sense, a holder of stock of a corporation`
    OR `the person is a member of the joint-stock association`
    OR `the person holds a share of stock or other evidence of financial or beneficial interest in the joint-stock association`

§§ `s 254(b) the power to merge or consolidate with a joint-stock association`

-- The surviving or resulting entity: a corporation of this State (a stock corporation or a nonstock corporation) or a
-- joint-stock association. "may be organized for profit or not organized for profit".
-- src:1149 | The surviving or resulting entity may be organized for profit or not organized for profit, and if the surviving or resulting entity is a corporation, it may be a stock corporation of this State or a nonstock corporation of this State.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 254(b) (src:1149)
GIVEN entity IS AN Entity
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 254(b) the entity may be the surviving or resulting entity` entity MEANS
    CONSIDER entity's `kind of entity`
    WHEN `a corporation` k                                  THEN `the entity was formed under the laws of this State` entity
    WHEN `a joint-stock association`                        THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a natural person`                                 THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a general partnership`                            THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a limited partnership`                            THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a limited liability partnership`                  THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a limited liability limited partnership`          THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a limited liability company`                      THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a statutory trust`                                THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a business trust or association`                  THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a real estate investment trust`                   THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a common-law trust`                               THEN FALSE
    WHEN `any other unincorporated business or association` THEN FALSE

-- src:1149 | Any 1 or more corporations of this State may merge or consolidate with 1 or more joint-stock associations, unless the laws of the jurisdiction or jurisdictions under which such joint-stock association or associations are formed or organized prohibit such merger or consolidation. Such corporation or corporations and such 1 or more joint-stock associations may merge into a single surviving corporation or joint-stock association, which may be any 1 of such corporations or joint-stock associations, or they may consolidate into a new resulting corporation of this State or a joint-stock association, pursuant to an agreement …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 254(b) (src:1149)
GIVEN kind                                                                            IS A `s 251 Kind of combination`
      `the number of constituent corporations that are corporations of this State`    IS A NUMBER
      `the number of constituent entities that are joint-stock associations`          IS A NUMBER
      `the laws of the jurisdiction under which a joint-stock association is formed or organized prohibit the merger or consolidation` IS A BOOLEAN -- out of range: the laws of the other jurisdictions
      `the surviving or resulting entity may be the surviving or resulting entity under s 254(b)` IS A BOOLEAN -- the rule `s 254(b) the entity may be the surviving or resulting entity`
      `the surviving entity is one of the constituent entities`                      IS A BOOLEAN
      `the agreement complies with s 254`                                             IS A BOOLEAN
      `the agreement is approved in accordance with s 254`                            IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 254(b) a corporation of this State may merge or consolidate with a joint-stock association` kind `the number of constituent corporations that are corporations of this State` `the number of constituent entities that are joint-stock associations` `the laws of the jurisdiction under which a joint-stock association is formed or organized prohibit the merger or consolidation` `the surviving or resulting entity may be the surviving or resulting entity under s 254(b)` `the surviving entity is one of the constituent entities` `the agreement complies with s 254` `the agreement is approved in accordance with s 254` MEANS
        `the number of constituent corporations that are corporations of this State` AT LEAST 1
    AND `the number of constituent entities that are joint-stock associations` AT LEAST 1
    AND (NOT `the laws of the jurisdiction under which a joint-stock association is formed or organized prohibit the merger or consolidation`)
    AND `the surviving or resulting entity may be the surviving or resulting entity under s 254(b)`
    AND (CONSIDER kind
         WHEN `a merger into a single surviving corporation`     THEN `the surviving entity is one of the constituent entities`
         WHEN `a consolidation into a new resulting corporation` THEN TRUE)
    AND `the agreement complies with s 254`
    AND `the agreement is approved in accordance with s 254`

§§ `s 254(c) the agreement`

-- One field per limb of (c)(1) to (c)(7). (c)(3) is for a merger "in which the surviving entity is a corporation of this State",
-- (c)(4) for a consolidation "in which the resulting entity is a corporation of this State".
-- src:1150 | (c) Each such corporation and joint-stock association shall enter into a written agreement of merger or consolidation. The agreement shall state:
-- src:1151 | (1) The terms and conditions of the merger or consolidation;
-- src:1152 | (2) The mode of carrying the same into effect;
-- src:1153 | In the case of a merger in which the surviving entity is a corporation of this State, such amendments or changes in the certificate of incorporation of the surviving corporation as are desired to be effected by the merger (which amendments or changes may amend and restate the certificate of incorporation of the surviving corporation in its entirety), or, if no such amendments or changes are desired, a statement that the certificate of incorporation of the surviving corporation shall be its certificate of incorporation;
-- src:1154 | (4) In the case of a consolidation in which the resulting entity is a corporation of this State, that the certificate of incorporation of the resulting corporation shall be as is set forth in an attachment to the agreement;
-- src:1155 | The manner, if any, of converting the shares of stock of each stock corporation, the interest of members of each nonstock corporation, and the shares, membership or financial or beneficial interests in each of the joint-stock associations into shares or other securities of a stock corporation or membership interests of a nonstock corporation or into shares, memberships or financial or beneficial interests of the joint-stock association surviving or resulting from such merger or consolidation, or of cancelling some or all of such shares, memberships or financial or beneficial interests, and, if any shares of any such stock corporation, any membership interests of any such nonstock corporation or any shares, memberships or financial or beneficial interests in any such joint-stock association are not to remain outstanding, to be converted solely into shares or other securities of the stock corporation or membership interests of the nonstock corporation or into shares, memberships or financial or beneficial interests of the joint-stock association surviving or resulting from such merger or consolidation or to be cancelled, the cash, property, rights or securities of any other corporation or entity which the holders of shares of any such stock corporation, membership interests of any such nonstock corporation, or shares, memberships or financial or beneficial interests of any such joint-stock association are to receive in exchange for, or upon conversion of such shares, membership interests or shares, memberships or financial or beneficial interests, and the surrender of any certificates evidencing them, which cash, property, rights or securities of any other corporation or entity may be in addition to or in lieu of shares or other securities of the stock corporation or membership interests of the nonstock corporation or shares, memberships or financial or beneficial interests of the joint-stock association surviving or resulting from such merger or consolidation;
-- src:1156 | Such other details or provisions as are deemed desirable, including, without limiting the generality of the foregoing, a provision for the payment of cash in lieu of the issuance or recognition of fractional shares, rights, other securities or interests of the surviving or resulting entity or of fractional shares, rights, other securities or interests of any other corporation or entity the securities of which are to be received in the merger or consolidation, or for some other arrangement with respect thereto, consistent with § 155 of this title; and
-- src:1157 | (7) Such other provisions or facts as shall be required to be set forth in an agreement of merger or consolidation (including any provision for amendment of the governing documents of a surviving joint-stock association) or required to establish and maintain a joint-stock association by the laws under which the joint-stock association is formed or organized.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 254(c)(1) to (7) (src:1150-1157)
DECLARE `s 254(c) Agreement of merger or consolidation` HAS
    `each such corporation and joint-stock association entered into a written agreement`            IS A BOOLEAN
    `states the terms and conditions of the merger or consolidation`                                IS A BOOLEAN
    `states the mode of carrying the merger or consolidation into effect`                           IS A BOOLEAN
    `states the amendments or changes in the certificate of incorporation of the surviving corporation, or that it stays as it is` IS A BOOLEAN
    `states that the certificate of incorporation of the resulting corporation is as set forth in an attachment` IS A BOOLEAN
    `some shares, membership interests or financial or beneficial interests are to be converted or cancelled` IS A BOOLEAN
    `states the manner of converting or cancelling them`                                            IS A BOOLEAN
    `some shares, membership interests or financial or beneficial interests are not to remain outstanding` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the holders of those are to receive cash, property, rights or securities of another corporation or entity` IS A BOOLEAN
    `states the cash, property, rights or securities of another corporation or entity that the holders are to receive` IS A BOOLEAN
    `contains a provision for cash in lieu of fractional shares, rights, other securities or interests` IS A BOOLEAN
    `that provision is consistent with s 155`                                                       IS A BOOLEAN -- out of range: section 155 (piece dg3)
    `states the other provisions or facts required to be set forth in an agreement of merger or consolidation, or required to establish and maintain a joint-stock association by the laws under which it is formed or organized` IS A BOOLEAN -- out of range: the laws of the other jurisdictions

