-- src:1153 | In the case of a merger in which the surviving entity is a corporation of this State, such amendments or changes in the certificate of incorporation of the surviving corporation as are desired to be effected by the merger (which amendments or changes may amend and restate the certificate of incorporation of the surviving corporation in its entirety), or, if no such amendments or changes are desired, a statement that the certificate of incorporation of the surviving corporation shall be its certificate of incorporation;
-- src:1154 | (4) In the case of a consolidation in which the resulting entity is a corporation of this State, that the certificate of incorporation of the resulting corporation shall be as is set forth in an attachment to the agreement;
-- src:1155 | The manner, if any, of converting the shares of stock of each stock corporation, the interest of members of each nonstock corporation, and the shares, membership or financial or beneficial interests in each of the joint-stock associations into shares or other securities of a stock corporation or membership interests of a nonstock corporation or into shares, memberships or financial or beneficial interests of the joint-stock association surviving or resulting from such merger or consolidation, or of cancelling some or all of such shares, memberships or financial or beneficial interests, and, if any shares of any such stock corporation, any membership interests of any such nonstock corporation or any shares, memberships or financial or beneficial interests in any such joint-stock association are not to remain outstanding, to be converted solely into shares or other securities of the stock corporation or membership interests of the nonstock corporation or into shares, memberships or financial or beneficial interests of the joint-stock association surviving or resulting from such merger or consolidation or to be cancelled, the cash, property, rights or securities of any other corporation or entity which the holders of shares of any such stock corporation, membership interests of any such nonstock corporation, or shares, memberships or financial or beneficial interests of any such joint-stock association are to receive in exchange for, or upon conversion of such shares, membership interests or shares, memberships or financial or beneficial interests, and the surrender of any certificates evidencing them, which cash, property, rights or securities of any other corporation or entity may be in addition to or in lieu of shares or other securities of the stock corporation or membership interests of the nonstock corporation or shares, memberships or financial or beneficial interests of the joint-stock association surviving or resulting from such merger or consolidation;
-- src:1157 | (7) Such other provisions or facts as shall be required to be set forth in an agreement of merger or consolidation (including any provision for amendment of the governing documents of a surviving joint-stock association) or required to establish and maintain a joint-stock association by the laws under which the joint-stock association is formed or organized.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 254(c)(1) to (7) (src:1150-1157)
GIVEN kind                                                                           IS A `s 251 Kind of combination`
      `the surviving or resulting entity is a corporation of this State`             IS A BOOLEAN
      agreement                                                                      IS A `s 254(c) Agreement of merger or consolidation`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 254(c) the agreement states what the subsection requires` kind `the surviving or resulting entity is a corporation of this State` agreement MEANS
        agreement's `each such corporation and joint-stock association entered into a written agreement`
    AND agreement's `states the terms and conditions of the merger or consolidation`
    AND agreement's `states the mode of carrying the merger or consolidation into effect`
    AND (CONSIDER kind
         WHEN `a merger into a single surviving corporation`
              THEN (    (NOT `the surviving or resulting entity is a corporation of this State`)
                     OR agreement's `states the amendments or changes in the certificate of incorporation of the surviving corporation, or that it stays as it is`)
         WHEN `a consolidation into a new resulting corporation`
              THEN (    (NOT `the surviving or resulting entity is a corporation of this State`)
                     OR agreement's `states that the certificate of incorporation of the resulting corporation is as set forth in an attachment`))
    AND (    (NOT agreement's `some shares, membership interests or financial or beneficial interests are to be converted or cancelled`)
          OR agreement's `states the manner of converting or cancelling them`)
    AND (    (NOT (    agreement's `some shares, membership interests or financial or beneficial interests are not to remain outstanding`
                   AND agreement's `the holders of those are to receive cash, property, rights or securities of another corporation or entity`))
          OR agreement's `states the cash, property, rights or securities of another corporation or entity that the holders are to receive`)
    AND agreement's `states the other provisions or facts required to be set forth in an agreement of merger or consolidation, or required to establish and maintain a joint-stock association by the laws under which it is formed or organized`

-- src:1156 | Such other details or provisions as are deemed desirable, including, without limiting the generality of the foregoing, a provision for the payment of cash in lieu of the issuance or recognition of fractional shares, rights, other securities or interests of the surviving or resulting entity or of fractional shares, rights, other securities or interests of any other corporation or entity the securities of which are to be received in the merger or consolidation, or for some other arrangement with respect thereto, consistent with § 155 of this title; and
@ref 8 Del. C. § 254(c)(6) (src:1156)
GIVEN agreement IS A `s 254(c) Agreement of merger or consolidation`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 254(c)(6) the agreement's provision for cash in lieu of fractions is permitted` agreement MEANS
        (NOT agreement's `contains a provision for cash in lieu of fractional shares, rights, other securities or interests`)
    OR agreement's `that provision is consistent with s 155`

-- src:1158 | Any of the terms of the agreement of merger or consolidation may be made dependent upon facts ascertainable outside of such agreement, provided that the manner in which such facts shall operate upon the terms of the agreement is clearly and expressly set forth in the agreement of merger or consolidation …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 254(c) closing paragraph (src:1158)
GIVEN `the agreement clearly and expressly sets forth the manner in which those facts operate upon the term` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 254(c) a term of the agreement may depend on facts ascertainable outside the agreement` `the agreement clearly and expressly sets forth the manner in which those facts operate upon the term` MEANS
    `the agreement clearly and expressly sets forth the manner in which those facts operate upon the term`

-- The sentence defining "facts" in section 254(c): the same words as in section 251(b), read the same way (NOTES.md fork register F26): an
-- event, or a determination or action by any person or body (the corporation too), is a fact; anything else, the text does not say.
-- src:1158 | The term “facts,” as used in the preceding sentence, includes, but is not limited to, the occurrence of any event, including a determination or action by any person or body, including the corporation.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 254(c) closing paragraph (src:1158)
GIVEN item IS A `s 251(b) Kind of item that a term may depend on`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 254(c) the item is a fact within the meaning of the closing paragraph` item MEANS
    CONSIDER item
    WHEN `an event, as the facts sentence of s 251(b) reads`                                                         THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `a determination or action by a person or body, including the corporation, as the facts sentence of s 251(b) reads` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `something else, which the facts sentence of s 251(b) neither names nor excludes`                          THEN NOTHING

